# RenPyLinter patch series for this engine branch.
#
# Format: <patch file> <where it is applied>
#   root          applied with `patch -p1` to the renpy-build checkout by
#                 tools/runtime (renpylinter/tooling) before any task runs
#   task:<module> applied by tasks/<module>.py to the unpacked source
#
# Every file in this directory except this one must be listed.

# Per-session Python heap in librenpython (plan 4.3 step 1 placement).
librenpython-session-zone.diff root

# libffi 3.4.5 aarch64 CFI order; Apple clang errors with "invalid CFI
# advance_loc expression". Upstream libffi 8308bed (#857), released in 3.4.7.
libffi-aarch64-cfi.diff task:libffi

# The Objective-C runtime's copy functions return memory the caller frees
# (objc/runtime.h); pyobjus kept none of it: method_copyReturnType and
# method_copyArgumentType strings for every method autoclass() reflects
# (2.15 MiB in one AfterClass session), and class_copyPropertyList's array.
# Also frees class_copyMethodList's array when a conversion raises.
pyobjus-free-runtime-copies.diff task:pyobjus

# pyobjus ObjcMethod.__call__ malloc's the ffi return-value buffer
# (res_ptr) for every Objective-C call and never freed it; it also leaked
# f_args and the argument buffers on the `return self.p_class` shortcut
# and on every exception. Free them all in a finally. The struct return
# branch of convert_cy_ret_to_py copied nothing (ctypes .contents aliased
# the buffer); it now returns a from_buffer_copy so the buffer can go.
pyobjus-free-call-result-buffer.diff task:pyobjus

# Ren'Py's ftfont / hbfont create a FreeType library in init() and never
# call FT_Done_FreeType. The handle is a module static that RenPyLinter
# zeroes between its in-process sessions, so one FT_Library plus its
# modules stayed on the default heap per session. Adds quit(), which the
# host's main.py calls at shutdown: it destroys the library at once when no
# face / font object is alive and otherwise from the last __dealloc__, so
# bitmaps, strokers and faces still go through FreeType.
renpy-freetype-quit.diff root

# pyobjus' autoclass() instantiates the class it builds and parks that
# instance in every ObjcMethod.p_class of the class, while the class sits
# in the module-static oclass_register that Py_Finalize never releases, so
# the Objective-C instance (SwiftBridge, UIDevice, AVSpeechSynthesizer, the
# last NSString a call returned, ...) was never released; the same
# instance <-> class cycle also pins any proxy Ren'Py keeps in a store or
# module global. Adds clear_autoclass_cache(), which drops every p_class
# and empties the registry, for the host's main.py to call before
# finalization.
pyobjus-clear-autoclass-cache.diff task:pyobjus

# pyobjus retained every object a method returned, but alloc, new...,
# copy..., mutableCopy... and init... already hand the caller a +1
# reference (Cocoa ownership; ARC's ns_returns_retained), so each
# alloc().init() proxy and each objc_str() leaked one retain count
# (AVSpeechSynthesizer grew by one per session with no Python proxy left,
# RenPyLinter-ios diagnostics/memory-2026-10-06-freetype-pyobjus-fix/run9).
# Wrap those results without retaining; when init returns a different
# object than its receiver (class clusters), the receiver proxy no longer
# releases what init consumed. Applied after the other pyobjus patches.
pyobjus-owned-returns.diff task:pyobjus
